**Designing a Storage Engine**

I'm focusing on a distributed time-series database design. It'll utilize a simple architecture with ingest routers, storage nodes, and query nodes, but I won't go with Postgres. Instead, I'll opt for a custom engine based on Log-Structured Merge-trees (LSM), using etcd for metadata. Key design choices include time-partitioned LSM segments, an inverted index for series ID mapping, and treating rollups as first-class. I’ll also address failure modes and operational challenges while setting scalability targets. Now it's time to craft the documentation!
